commons shop.values

---
A product's stock-keeping unit. Opaque, so a sku can't be passed where an
order id is expected, although both are strings.
---
type Sku = opaque String where NonEmpty

---
The id the customer chooses for an order, from the URL.
---
type OrderId = opaque String where NonEmpty

---
How many units of one sku an order moves.
---
type Quantity = Int where InRange(1, 1000)

---
A price in cents: at least one cent, at most 100,000.00.
---
type Cents = Int where InRange(1, 10000000)

---
Non-empty text: what a `Sku` or an `OrderId` is made of.
---
type Label = String where NonEmpty

---
A sku from text already known to be non-empty, so no `Result` is
needed. Only this commons may call `.unsafe`, and `Label` has already
established the predicate.
---
fn skuFrom(text: Label) -> Sku {
	Sku.unsafe(text)
}

---
An order id from non-empty text, as `skuFrom`.
---
fn orderIdFrom(text: Label) -> OrderId {
	OrderId.unsafe(text)
}

---
The order id as plain text. Only this commons can read an `OrderId`'s
string; the shop's stores key their maps by it, and keep the `OrderId`
itself in the value.
---
fn orderRef(id: OrderId) -> String {
	id.raw
}

---
The sku as plain text, for a map key, as `orderRef`.
---
fn skuRef(s: Sku) -> String {
	s.raw
}
